  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "According to the Shader Blocking System documentation, shaders containing \"Toon\" should be replaced with \"Toon/Lit\", and I remember it working that way in the past.\nHowever, when I checked VRChat recently (10/28/2021), it seems to have been replaced by another shader that is neither \"Toon/Lit\" nor \"Standard\".\nThat shader can use real-time shadows, and draws flat shades similar to \"Toon/Lit\". What is this shader?\nAlso, if the rules for the Shader Blocking System have changed, it would be nice if the documentation could be updated at some point.\nReference: https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/shader-fallback-system",
